{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 126, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip where no direct input-output path exists creates a new residual path, which gains much more than replacing an existing op (13,14,20-22 vs 17-19)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct skip, removing edge 0 can nearly disconnect the cell and collapse accuracy (31,32 vs 23)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When e1 is absent, node 1 via e0 is the only route into nodes 2/3 beyond the skip, so removing e0 hurts far more (30,31)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With e4 removed, e5 is the main conv path to the output, so deleting it is catastrophic (64,65 vs 61,62)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on e4 supplies a near-identity route to the output that is otherwise missing when e3 is none (82,88,90 vs 81,83)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a direct skip, adding a skip on e1 provides a short gradient path and helps instead of slightly hurting (94 vs 91,93)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an absent edge with a conv adds a new computation path, which beats swapping out an existing op (4,6,11,12 vs 79,80)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring a missing first edge reactivates node 1's contributions, gaining more than replacing another op on e0 (75 vs 76-78)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5